{
 "_about": "Rudyard Kipling (1865-1936): every book of his this house holds, and the completeness note. Adam asked 2026-11-03: \"Give me a kippling shelf\". Prose (`gutenberg`) is fetched by fetch_sources.py from the GITenberg mirror of Project Gutenberg, pinned to a commit and a sha256, and built by structure_texts.py into data/books/<slug>.json (gitignored), so the Armarium shows each as a book. Verse (`poetry_hoard`) lives in the Poetry Hoard as whole volumes and reaches the Armarium bound as volumes; it is listed here so every Kipling work has one uid from one place. Each row's `citation` (kipling:<work>) and `uid` are minted by build_kipling_shelf.py. RIGHTS: every book here was first published in 1930 or before, so it is public domain in the US; each Gutenberg header was read for 'COPYRIGHTED Project Gutenberg' (none). The 1923 and 1926 books were renewed (Stanford renewals database: R62719, R70384, R69256 ...) and are free by the 95-year term all the same.",
